Z||000000||ChadMan||09-16-2001||09:34 PM||||Well, today I pulled the steering rack out of the Coupe, removed the old inner tie rod ends, greased the shaft (snicker), installed a new rack bushing and inner tie rod ends from Rodney Dickman and my 1-week-old outers from AutoZone, and reinstalled.<P>Sounds easy, but it took me all day!  I broke off three of the studs that hold the rack to the frame and had to knock out the old tack-welded nuts with a cold chisel.  Thanks to EVERYONE who gave me advice on this project!<P>The alignment (or lack thereof) is downright spooky, but the front end is solid as a rock over railroad tracks, bumps in turns, etc.  I'll be calling a front-end shop tomorrow morning to get things straightened out.<P>Hopefully I will be back at the autocross track next month!<BR>||||reg||10
